DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T120000
UID:27d5ffaadbf57ec4418337a09b26159d@tbn.ca
DESCRIPTION:The Rouge National Urban Park is a rich assembly of natural\, 
 cultural and agricultural landscapes. It is home to amazing biodiversity a
 nd some of the last remaining working farms in the Greater Toronto Area. I
 t houses Toronto's only campground\, one of the regions largest marshes an
 d amazing hiking opportunities. This is the best time to be hiking because
  the leaves will either be changing or will have changed. NOTE: WE HAVE HA
 D ISSUES WITH PARKING IN THE PAST SO ARRIVE EARLY. START TIME IS 9 AM. Ple
 ase Register - Only REGISTRANTS are permitted to participate in this event
 . Not a member but you want to try this out? Sign up for our 30 Day Trial 
 membership and you can try out multiple TBN even...
URL:https://www.tbn.ca/widget/event-6851941
X-SOURCE:Toronto Bicycling Network
